=== Entry gate: the factorisation contract ===

At r = 0 with diagonal Phi, Theta and Sigma the likelihood factorises,
so the joint fit must equal the sum of the univariate fits exactly.

  univariate 1 (p=2, q=1)   logL =     -20.0579540511
  univariate 2 (p=2, q=1)   logL =     -14.5692106917
                                 sum  =     -34.6271647428
                                 joint=     -34.6271647428
  (both sides untruncated; the fit's own logL, xi truncated at 1e-03, is -34.6271860868)

  crossing identity (joint - sum) = -9.948e-14   (tolerance 1.0e-06)   VERIFIED
  rung 1  (F diag, Theta diag, Sigma free)   logL = -30.5490766364
  rung 2  (F free, Theta free, Sigma free)   logL = 1.6047465592

